<h2 class="mb-3">Background</h2>
<p>Kijura Town Council was established on <strong>1 July 2010</strong> when it was carved out of Hakibale Sub-County in Burahya County, Kabarole District. The establishment was made under the Local Government Act, with the primary objective of bringing government services closer to the people and promoting local development.</p>
<p>The town council is strategically located along the Fort Portal–Mubende Highway, approximately 30 km north-east of Fort Portal City, making it an important transit and trade centre in the district. The area has historically been associated with tea growing, with TAMTECO and Kamusanga Tea Factories being key economic anchors in the region.</p>
<p>Since its establishment, Kijura Town Council has worked to improve infrastructure, service delivery, revenue mobilization and community welfare through collaboration with development partners, government agencies and local communities.</p>
